# EIAMS frontend — canonical development environment table
#
# Two mutually exclusive profiles exist. This file documents both; the values
# below are the defaults and select the real-backend profile.
#
# | Profile      | VITE_AUTH_BYPASS | Proves                          |
# | ------------ | ---------------- | ------------------------------- |
# | real-backend | false (default)  | real integration (the default)   |
# | ui-sandbox   | true             | UI work only — NOT integration   |
#
# RESOLUTION-040: real backend integration is the default. Disabling the
# fixture alone is NOT proof of the real authentication flow, because the auth
# fixture used to default to on. A fixture-backed session cannot answer for
# login, refresh, authorization or session hydration, so a UI sandbox is opt-in
# and is visibly marked in the shell.
#
# There is no development API-mock flag any more. `VITE_ENABLE_API_MOCKS` and
# the `src/mocks/` MSW browser worker it started were removed in
# `eiams-frontend-m4jm` (EPIC G7): a mock layer reachable from the app
# bootstrap is a fixture able to answer a real request. The MSW harness under
# `src/test/msw/` remains and is test-only — Vitest boots it, the app never
# imports it.

# Origin-relative on purpose: the browser must stay same-origin so the host-only
# refresh cookie is delivered and sent without cross-origin access, and the
# production HTTPS host can proxy /api/v1 itself.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1

# Replaces /auth/refresh with a fixture session. OFF by default, and a
# production build that enables it refuses to boot.
VITE_AUTH_BYPASS=false

# Development-only API proxy target, read by the Vite dev server and never
# exposed to browser code. Deliberately not VITE_-prefixed so the backend
# origin cannot reach the client bundle. The dev server forwards the configured
# API path (default /api/v1) to this origin so the browser stays same-origin.
# Defaults to http://localhost:5000 when unset; override in .env.local.
# EIAMS_DEV_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:5000
#
# To work without a backend, opt into the sandbox explicitly, e.g. in .env.local:
#   VITE_AUTH_BYPASS=true
#
# What the auth bypass actually does, and what it never did:
#
#   It answers POST /auth/refresh client-side with a fixture session, and marks
#   the shell so a fixture-authenticated UI is never mistaken for integration
#   evidence. It is the WHOLE sandbox now: there is no second half to enable.
#
#   The deleted mock layer used to be that second half, and it never provided a
#   session of its own — `src/mocks/handlers.ts` had no GET /auth/session and no
#   POST /auth/refresh handler, only POST /auth/logout (204). That is why both
#   flags used to be needed, and why removing the mock half leaves the auth
#   bypass sufficient rather than making the sandbox weaker.
#
# See docs/development-environment-profiles.md for the full rationale.